    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** leading our projections at 69.33, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Abbott. Despite the platoon disadvantage, his elite speed profile and top-of-the-order positioning make him a premium asset for our stolen base-focused strategy. **Casey Schmitt** also presents as a high-upside play at 63.92; his dynamic platoon advantage against the right-handed Lorenzen and a favorable order placement provide the structural support for a breakout performance. Meanwhile, **Kazuma Okamoto** rounds out our top-tier targets at 61.40, as he is uniquely positioned to feast on M\u00e1rquez\u2019s 5.58 xERA, benefiting significantly from his spot in the cleanup position.\n\nThe lineup construction was finalized by a narrow margin at the utility slot, where **Junior Caminero** (58.35) edged out **Carson Benge** (43.14). While **Carson Benge** was in the conversation, the optimizer favored **Junior Caminero**\u2019s superior xwOBA and dynamic platoon edge against Hancock to maintain our efficiency floor. We remain cautious regarding the top of our lineup; **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** face a significant hurdle in Skubal (2.69 xERA). While their raw talent and order placement keep them as \"Strong\" plays, the difficulty of the matchup suppresses their ceiling. Additionally, while **Christian Yelich** faces the formidable Skenes, his +13% platoon edge keeps him firmly in the lineup, though he represents a volatility risk given the opposing arm\u2019s dominance. We continue to bench **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, and **Lars Nootbaar**, as all three fell below the 40.0 efficiency floor due to prohibitive matchups against elite-tier starting pitching.",
